# fixedbugs, defect 2466, lane b31-ffi, 2026-11-11: the group says `link
# "m"`, and its header declares a name the library this build links for `m`
# does not define. Until this defect the missing name was told as one no
# group names a library for, *no group in this program says which library
# has it*, its note to write the `link` already written; it is told now by
# the library the group names, the note naming the two causes the linker's
# line cannot tell apart.
extern "own.h" link "m"
    function heroes_2466_absent(x: f64) -> f64  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(heroes_2466_absent(x: 2.0))
